Dear Shelley

Thank you for your patience, and yes, the visit went well. Abel completed a f=
ull RF survey of the property, and I have attached our proposal based on that=
 work.

In short, we are recommending that Barefoot Addo owns its own private wireles=
s network rather than continuing to rent one. The proposal covers:

- What we found on site, including the current mounting structure and the cov=
erage gap at the spa
- The proposed build: a new engineered mast, two sector radios covering the f=
ull property, and 28 connection points (including the spa, connected for the =
first time)
- Why reliability matters here: guest experience, day-to-day operations, and =
after-hours security, with the network designed for 99.9% availability
- The investment, with the full scope of what is included
- The financial case: monthly cost against the current setup, payback period,=
 and the five-year position
- The order of work, and why the Vodacom link goes in last

This is offered on a 36-month agreement. I should also mention we have secure=
d the equipment for this build with our supplier, and wireless stock does tig=
hten at this time of year - no pressure intended, just so you have the full p=
icture.

I would welcome the chance to walk the owners through it, whether in person o=
r by video call, as I know they are not based locally.

Please let me know if there is anything you would like clarified, and I am ha=
ppy to arrange a time that suits.

Kind regards

